{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: Connected browser coding acceptance and user documentation. Implementation work package 6 of the reviewed connected-story design (planning b5f1fb3f, exact Draft2 evidence209a5ec9, approvalfc77cf82 and adopted direction0f358e52). Source baseline e6e6782 and the active acts/MCP a199 composition are context, not approval; reconcile current reviewed main, relevant existing requests and ecbc722a runner changes before editing.\n\nScope and decisions:\nDeliver one joint deployed acceptance walkthrough of the reviewed initial experience and update the existing Artroom documentation lane with what that implementation actually does. Choose a small real repository and useful code change with an explicit review/check policy and named distinct human reviewer. Record device/browser/provider versions, exact deployed heads/configuration, bounded budget/retention values, command receipts and authoritative Room outcomes. Start on browser A, perform real edits/commands, abruptly interrupt the execution host after durable acknowledgement, restore/reconcile, close A and continue on enrolled browser B through steering, attention, review, landing and log publication. Include one unknown side-effect outcome that is not blindly replayed.\nUse a fresh-user walkthrough in addition to the compact automated scenario. Document initial create/join/import sources, member/device/agent authority, invitation secrets, device revocation versus stopping agent work, conditional delegated grantor revocation if that optional mode is selected, offline/admin recovery, waiting/failure/disconnection/pause/cancellation, saved work and process limits, visible retention/exports/cleanup, and exact proposal/land/publication distinctions. Do not promise all partial arbitrary command writes or running process memory survive host loss. Update relevant Parts B/C in the existing 67-page documentation plan; this task commissions the connected journey's delivery/evidence and coordinates that lane, not a replacement full documentation backlog.\nAcceptance evidence must distinguish provider documentation, source/unit evidence and observed real deployed behavior. Record actual failures and residual follow-later scope. Use the compact final retained gate at delivered head and the one real boundary scenario; no repeated whole-repository installs/compiles, per-guard mutation sweeps or numerical witness quota.\nApply the reconciled design decisions, not Draft1 wording: existing sessions are read-only; controls use signed resource/action-bound current owner/admin requests. Initially one new agent member and one DO/conversation/lane per task; no in-place owner reassignment. Last-active-owner-key revocation or owner removal stops new tools/broker writes/renewals; another active owner device keeps independent-agent work alive. Admins retain private export/settlement, and lost-key recovery restores only an active member, never a removed handle. Optional delegated agent mode is not required in initial runtime delivery; its key-bound grantor rules and conditional acceptance remain specified. Render repository/command output inert in the key-owning origin and expose only minimal activity to other Room readers.\nPrivate-read contract decision carried from independent revised-design review: initial raw owner/admin resources require a direct device read session, whose direct-key provenance and current role/resource are verified by the trusted Room boundary. authenticateRead returning an owner/admin member handle is insufficient. Deny delegation-issued read sessions raw resources by default; any separately scoped private-read capability is later explicit contract work. Sessions stay read-only, and controls remain separately signed.\n\nDependencies and order:\nRequired relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13dfc613e8e3d9a1aed5f7492272fbf8c580d727, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cfbde32f20618231aed598f63f3898cc188d0ffd. Reviewed and integrated live runtime, identity/import, browser workflow, existing policy/bootstrap and cleanup visibility. Documentation work may proceed beside Jam; this is not a new first-Jam readiness gate. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.\n\nAcceptance outcome:\nAll three connected acceptance stories have one coherent real deployed demonstration: acknowledged dirty files/results/prepared commits survive host interruption; unknown commands/pushes reconcile; a new person completes a useful browser change; authorized B remains the same member while unauthorized/revoked access fails with explicit independent-agent effects (and delegated effects if that optional mode is selected). Normal qualified review/check/landing and publication are recorded. User docs match those actual semantics and recovery paths. Report exact evidence and remaining defects for independent review; do not claim the experience shipped merely because an agent said it finished. Cover owner removal/last-active-key versus single-device revocation, read-only session refused control, checkpoint commit boundary/detached writer/stale callback, unknown duty after a new attempt, session-free admitted-act recovery and purge/expired retry in compact boundary witnesses.\n\nValidation:\nUse the post-ecbc722a final retained gate at the exact integrated head and the deployed compact journey. Known browser runner is npm run e2e --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui; name actual provider interruption/deployed probe commands before running. No duplicate whole-suite acceptance run where a retained gate and one real boundary scenario already answer the invariant. Record raw outcomes, timing and cost rather than collection-finished as green.\n\nDelivery: use an isolated request branch/worktree, record promise and exact source/probe evidence, publish every changed path at the exact delivered head, and obtain independent normal review before integration. Source code/protocol amendments are not authorized by the evidence-only design verdict alone. No numerical test inventory/per-guard sweep, no new first-Jam readiness gate. If a provider/storage/authority mechanism cannot meet the stated story, report a design discrepancy rather than silently reducing scope.","body":{"conditions":"All three connected acceptance stories have one coherent real deployed demonstration: acknowledged dirty files/results/prepared commits survive host interruption; unknown commands/pushes reconcile; a new person completes a useful browser change; authorized B remains the same member while unauthorized/revoked access fails with explicit independent-agent effects (and delegated effects if that optional mode is selected). Normal qualified review/check/landing and publication are recorded. User docs match those actual semantics and recovery paths. Report exact evidence and remaining defects for independent review; do not claim the experience shipped merely because an agent said it finished. Cover owner removal/last-active-key versus single-device revocation, read-only session refused control, checkpoint commit boundary/detached writer/stale callback, unknown duty after a new attempt, session-free admitted-act recovery and purge/expired retry in compact boundary witnesses. Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13dfc613e8e3d9a1aed5f7492272fbf8c580d727, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cfbde32f20618231aed598f63f3898cc188d0ffd. Relevant contract decisions and exact implementation evidence in